spans.s:
1. रुष् (cf. √ रुश्) cl. 1. 4. P. (Dhātup. xvii, 42; xxvi, 120) रोषति or रुष्यति (rarely ˚ते, and रुषति, cf. रुषत्; Gr. also pf. रुरोष; aor. अरुषत् or अरोषीत्; fut. रोषिता, रोष्टा; रोषिष्यति; inf. रोषितुम् or रोष्टुम्; ind.p. रुष्य, MBh.),
to hurt, injure, kill (हिंसायाम्), Dhātup.;
 (cl. 1.) to be hurt or offended by, take offence (acc.), RV. viii, 99, 4;
to displease, be disagreeable to (gen.), ib. viii, 4, 8; AitBr. iv, 10 (cf. रुषत् and 1. रुशत्);
 cl. 4. to be vexed or cross, be angry with (gen.), MBh.; R. &c.:
Caus. (or cl. 10. Dhātup. xxxii, 131) रोषयति, ˚ते (aor. अरूरुषत्; Pass. रोष्यते),
to vex, annoy, displease, irritate, exasperate, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to be furious or angry, Divyāv. :
Desid. रुरुषिषति, रुरोषिषति Gr.:
Intens. रोरुष्यते, रोरोष्टि, ib. [cf. Gk. λύσσα &c.]

cl. 1. P. रूषति, to adorn, decorate, Dhātup. xvii, 27;
to cover, strew, smear (see रूषित) :
Caus. (or cl. 10. P.) रूषयति, ‘to tremble’ or ‘to burst’ (विस्फुरणे), Dhātup. xxxv, 84; Vop.
